.Dd June 5, 2026
.Dt MAC_CAPABILITY_IDENTITY 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac_capability_identity
.Nd MAC_CAPABILITY program identity queries
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load at boot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo 'mac_capability_identity_load="YES"' >> /boot/loader.conf
.Ed
.Pp
Wire protocol header:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <dev/mac_capability/mac_capability_identity_proto.h>
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
service provides program nonce queries via
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL .
The service is registered under the name
.Dq identity .
.Pp
A program nonce is an 8-byte cryptographic random value that identifies
a program image.
The nonce is inherited across
.Xr fork 2
and rotated on
.Xr execve 2 .
Zero is never a valid nonce.
.Pp
The identity fd can be freely passed to sandboxed children so they can
discover their own identity.
No privilege is required to connect.
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width "IDENTITY_OP_QUERY"
.It Dv IDENTITY_OP_SELF Pq 1
Returns the caller's own program nonce.
No fd attachment is needed.
.It Dv IDENTITY_OP_QUERY Pq 2
Returns the program nonce of the process referenced by an attached
.Xr procdesc 4
file descriptor.
The procdesc fd must be attached to the
.Dv MAC_CAPABILITY_CALL .
.El
.Ss Wire Structures
.Bd -literal -offset indent
struct identity_request {
	uint32_t  op;         /* IDENTITY_OP_SELF or IDENTITY_OP_QUERY */
	uint32_t  _reserved;
} __packed;

struct identity_reply {
	uint32_t  status;
	uint32_t  _pad;
	uint64_t  nonce;
} __packed;
.Ed
.Ss Status Codes
.Bl -column "Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_DEAD" "Value" -offset indent
.It Sy Constant Ta Sy Value
.It Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_OK Ta 0
.It Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_ERR Ta 1
.It Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_DEAD Ta 2
.El
.Pp
.Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_OK
indicates success; the
.Fa nonce
field contains the result.
.Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_ERR
indicates the nonce could not be retrieved (e.g., no nonce assigned).
.Dv IDENTITY_STATUS_DEAD
indicates the process referenced by the attached procdesc has exited.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EINVAL
Request too small, reply buffer too small, invalid operation code,
no fd attached for
.Dv IDENTITY_OP_QUERY ,
or the attached fd is not a procdesc.
.El
.Pp
Application-level errors are returned in the
.Fa status
field of
.Vt struct identity_reply .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr execve 2 ,
.Xr fork 2 ,
.Xr mac_capability 4 ,
.Xr procdesc 4 ,
.Xr authorityd 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
